Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Visoto depends on the following third-party software. None of it is
redistributed in this repository: Go modules are fetched by the toolchain
(see go.mod / go.sum) and the browser libraries below are loaded from a public
CDN at runtime. Each remains under its own license, listed here for
attribution.

Front-end libraries (loaded from a CDN at runtime)

  Tabler                  1.4.0    MIT         https://tabler.io
  Tabulator               6.5.2    MIT         https://tabulator.info
  Graph Explorer          2.1.0    LGPL-2.1    https://github.com/zazuko/graph-explorer
    A fork of Ontodia, Copyright (c) metaphacts GmbH. Loaded unmodified from
    the CDN as a separate work; Visoto links to it from the browser and does
    not incorporate or modify its source.
  htmx                    2.0.10   BSD-2-Clause  https://htmx.org
  Lucide                  1.37.0   ISC         https://lucide.dev
  Chart.js                4.5.1    MIT         https://www.chartjs.org
  chartjs-adapter-date-fns 3.0.0   MIT         https://github.com/chartjs/chartjs-adapter-date-fns
  Wunderbaum              0.14.1   MIT         https://mar10.github.io/wunderbaum/
  highlight.js            11.12.0  BSD-3-Clause  https://highlightjs.org
  SheetJS (xlsx)          0.18.5   Apache-2.0  https://sheetjs.com
  svg-pan-zoom            3.6.2    BSD-2-Clause  https://github.com/bumbu/svg-pan-zoom

Go modules

  Direct and transitive dependencies are declared in go.mod and pinned in
  go.sum. They are predominantly MIT- and BSD-licensed; run
  `go list -m all` to enumerate the full set.

Ontologies

  The RDF vocabularies under ontologies/ (RDF, RDFS, OWL, Dublin Core) are
  published by the W3C and DCMI under their respective open terms.
